 The multi-axial archetype identifier identifies archetypes in a global concept space within a given namespace. It is also known as an 'ontological' identifier, since the concept space can be understood as an ontology of informational concepts on which the archetypes are based. The syntax of the identifier is described in the {openehr_base_artefact_identification}[openEHR Artefact Identification Specification^]. The structure of the concept space is essentially two-level, with the first level being a reference model class (e.g. openEHR `OBSERVATION` class) and the second being a domain concept (e.g. 'haematology result').
 
